WEBVTT

00:00:00.721 --> 00:00:04.433
We've been dragging Matter bait with us.

00:00:04.642 --> 00:00:05.935
So it seems.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.686
There must be some mistake!

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.231
Earlier, I heard her say exactly that.

00:00:10.314 --> 00:00:15.444
In the last battle log,
the Matter's activity was following her.

00:00:15.694 --> 00:00:18.781
And then there's
this carbon nanostructure reaction.

00:00:19.156 --> 00:00:21.951
Proof her body
is made of artificial organisms.

00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:25.037
You must be kidding!

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:26.664
What's more,

00:00:27.164 --> 00:00:29.959
you're just fine outside without a suit.

00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:32.127
What are you hiding?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.718
Kanzaki...

00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:21.445
Why is everyone here?

00:02:24.573 --> 00:02:25.658
This...

00:02:26.158 --> 00:02:27.576
It's not what you think!

00:02:27.743 --> 00:02:29.703
It's okay, Tachibana.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:30.913
Kanzaki!

00:02:30.996 --> 00:02:34.249
There's nothing okay about it!
I want an explanation!

00:02:36.335 --> 00:02:37.419
Relax, Misawa.

00:02:38.003 --> 00:02:39.671
It's just as Seri said.

00:02:40.005 --> 00:02:43.801
Everything except Aiko's brain
is made of artificial organisms.

00:02:45.135 --> 00:02:49.431
Her body is made up of coexisting
real and artificial parts,

00:02:49.807 --> 00:02:51.183
a composite body.

00:02:52.226 --> 00:02:55.687
As you know,
composite bodies attract Matter.

00:02:55.771 --> 00:02:57.064
That can't be!

00:02:57.147 --> 00:03:00.025
Why didn't you tell us
something so important?!

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:02.778
You're right, it's a big problem.

00:03:03.112 --> 00:03:05.030
However, Aiko has been

00:03:05.114 --> 00:03:08.784
regularly injected with drugs
to neutralize those properties.

00:03:09.368 --> 00:03:10.577
She's no danger.

00:03:11.078 --> 00:03:12.705
Then there's no problem!

00:03:12.788 --> 00:03:15.040
This isn't Aiko's fault! See?

00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:16.750
Of course it is!

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:18.710
We've been attacked like crazy!

00:03:18.961 --> 00:03:19.795
Shino.

00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:20.879
Yes?

00:03:21.839 --> 00:03:25.384
You knew the girl was not normal.

00:03:25.843 --> 00:03:30.222
But do you have proof those drugs
kept her from attracting the Matter?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.812
I understand very clearly now.

00:03:36.937 --> 00:03:38.480
What the hell?

00:03:38.605 --> 00:03:40.983
Tell us it's not true, Aiko!

00:03:43.527 --> 00:03:44.820
I'm sorry!

00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:46.155
Aiko...

00:03:46.947 --> 00:03:49.825
I...

00:03:51.243 --> 00:03:53.412
I've been...

00:03:53.495 --> 00:03:54.663
Stop!

00:03:54.955 --> 00:03:57.750
It wasn't her who wanted
to hide this from you.

00:03:58.041 --> 00:04:00.419
I decided that keeping it secret

00:04:00.502 --> 00:04:02.129
was better for the mission.

00:04:03.172 --> 00:04:06.800
You son of a bitch!
We're putting our lives on the line!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.095
How dare you hire us
without telling us about all the risks!

00:04:10.721 --> 00:04:12.514
I'm doing it to end the Burst.

00:04:12.598 --> 00:04:13.432
What?

00:04:14.475 --> 00:04:17.394
Her real body is at Primary Point.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.648
If her two bodies are switched,
it will end the Burst.

00:04:22.065 --> 00:04:24.526
Switch her bodies?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.527
What?

00:04:25.736 --> 00:04:27.446
Explain your reasoning.

00:04:27.529 --> 00:04:29.740
You believe him, Haruka?

00:04:29.823 --> 00:04:30.866
Aiko?

00:04:32.951 --> 00:04:37.122
I decided to go to Ground Zero
for that purpose.

00:04:37.873 --> 00:04:40.501
You're serious?

00:04:41.084 --> 00:04:44.171
My mother and brother
are waiting to be rescued.

00:04:44.797 --> 00:04:46.799
Hey! That's right!

00:04:46.882 --> 00:04:48.926
We have to save Aiko's family!

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:50.969
You believe that?

00:04:51.094 --> 00:04:52.638
-It's the truth.
-What?

00:04:53.222 --> 00:04:55.516
Like what just happened to Tachibana,

00:04:55.724 --> 00:04:58.477
they're living inside of a cocoon.

00:04:59.228 --> 00:05:01.355
We can even monitor their situation.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.820
This is the reason you're being paid
a reward beyond anything you've heard of.

00:05:08.278 --> 00:05:10.072
We're going in there

00:05:10.364 --> 00:05:14.535
to stop the Burst and put an end
to this whole thing.

00:05:15.035 --> 00:05:18.288
Please! We need you for this!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:23.836
All right.

00:05:24.503 --> 00:05:27.339
We'll go as far as we can
for the job we took.

00:05:27.422 --> 00:05:29.299
-Sagami!
-Hey!

00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:30.259
However,

00:05:30.842 --> 00:05:34.721
if you hide anything else from us,
or if we get stuck,

00:05:35.097 --> 00:05:36.848
in order to protect my team,

00:05:37.307 --> 00:05:39.893
I'll kill you two myself.

00:05:44.565 --> 00:05:46.775
<i>-Doctor!</i>
<i>-Dr. Kiryu!</i>

00:05:47.985 --> 00:05:51.405
Time of death, 8:12 p.m.

00:05:53.198 --> 00:05:58.120
Dr. Kiryu brought us
the invaluable Cell Assembler.

00:05:58.203 --> 00:06:01.456
Then, he used his own body to prove

00:06:02.374 --> 00:06:04.960
Cell Assembler Two is effective

00:06:05.335 --> 00:06:10.007
in bringing about long life without
suffering and other further advances.

00:06:10.841 --> 00:06:14.261
Using artificial organisms
to advance medical practices--

00:06:14.386 --> 00:06:16.263
that is our mission.

00:06:17.973 --> 00:06:19.558
<i>Dr. Kiryu has died.</i>

00:06:19.683 --> 00:06:20.809
<i>So I hear.</i>

00:06:20.892 --> 00:06:22.269
<i>News travels fast.</i>

00:06:22.477 --> 00:06:25.814
<i>The new lab director</i>
<i>paid me a visit himself.</i>

00:06:26.315 --> 00:06:27.649
Isazu did?

00:06:27.941 --> 00:06:29.943
<i>This is such terrible timing.</i>

00:06:30.235 --> 00:06:31.320
Terrible timing?

00:06:31.695 --> 00:06:32.613
-<i>So?</i>
-What?

00:06:32.904 --> 00:06:34.990
<i>That's not why you called, right?</i>

00:06:35.073 --> 00:06:36.617
You're as blunt as ever.

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:38.785
We've found data showing

00:06:38.869 --> 00:06:43.332
a link between the Matter's activity
and Yuzuha Isazu's brainwaves.

00:06:43.665 --> 00:06:46.168
Yuzuha? How is that possible?

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.962
How is a comatose patient
linked to the Matter?

00:06:49.046 --> 00:06:50.714
<i>I can't explain why,</i>

00:06:50.922 --> 00:06:53.842
<i>but a few minutes </i>
<i>before the Matter turns active,</i>

00:06:53.925 --> 00:06:56.595
<i>her brainwaves start showing activity.</i>

00:06:56.845 --> 00:06:59.389
<i>I'm almost certain Isazu realizes this.</i>

00:07:00.015 --> 00:07:02.017
You mean he has kept it a secret?

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:06.229
<i>You said the timing was terrible.</i>
<i>What did you mean by that?</i>

00:07:06.355 --> 00:07:08.482
Thanks for this useful information.

00:07:08.565 --> 00:07:10.776
Tell me if you find anything else.

00:07:10.859 --> 00:07:11.735
<i>Hey!</i>

00:07:14.321 --> 00:07:17.574
<i>Hori, tell all the companies</i>
<i>with facilities in AMBREC</i>

00:07:17.783 --> 00:07:22.537
<i>that the government is looking into</i>
<i>how to end this situation.</i>

00:07:22.788 --> 00:07:24.039
<i>This will heavily impact</i>

00:07:24.122 --> 00:07:26.708
<i>the integrity of samples</i>
<i>still in the Area.</i>

00:07:26.792 --> 00:07:28.502
<i>That's all. It's urgent!</i>

00:07:29.503 --> 00:07:30.629
-Close!
-Close!

00:07:42.432 --> 00:07:43.266
Tachibana!

00:07:56.571 --> 00:08:00.492
Like I thought, attacks on the Matter
affect her pain receptors.

00:08:00.575 --> 00:08:01.827
I'll get painkillers.

00:08:06.289 --> 00:08:08.834
Kanzaki!

00:08:09.418 --> 00:08:10.335
Tachibana!

00:08:12.671 --> 00:08:14.589
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR

00:08:31.606 --> 00:08:35.485
It looks like Dr. Isazu
won't be visiting you again today.

00:08:36.486 --> 00:08:37.612
It can't be helped.

00:08:37.988 --> 00:08:40.949
He's the hospital's
top-ranking person, after all.

00:08:43.368 --> 00:08:45.579
You must be lonely, Yuzuha.

00:08:47.539 --> 00:08:51.543
The track on the new rail system ahead
is blocked by the Matter.

00:08:51.626 --> 00:08:52.961
The Beetle can't pass.

00:08:53.045 --> 00:08:55.672
Proceed along the valley floor.
Be on high alert!

00:08:58.759 --> 00:09:01.928
Thank you, Shinoyama,.

00:09:02.304 --> 00:09:04.514
Thank you for convincing the Divers.

00:09:04.806 --> 00:09:06.016
It wasn't me.

00:09:06.183 --> 00:09:08.268
You should be thanking Sagami.

00:09:08.643 --> 00:09:12.147
The others only went along
because of what he said.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.150
Don't make that face.

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:17.486
They're a great team.

00:09:17.569 --> 00:09:20.947
And Shiraishi and I know
the importance of this mission.

00:09:22.115 --> 00:09:24.534
There's a purpose to what we're doing.

00:09:26.244 --> 00:09:27.412
<i>My old workplace.</i>

00:09:27.788 --> 00:09:30.665
<i>We can find</i>
<i>chemicals for our cartridges here.</i>

00:09:31.124 --> 00:09:34.002
<i>This place is incredible!</i>
<i>You worked here, Seri?</i>

00:09:35.087 --> 00:09:36.379
Sagami and Minase,

00:09:36.463 --> 00:09:38.548
I want you on patrol.

00:09:42.135 --> 00:09:44.346
We'll stand guard outside.

00:09:44.888 --> 00:09:47.099
I'll just get irritated in here, anyway.

00:09:47.182 --> 00:09:50.769
Come on! Let's take a break, Haruka!

00:09:51.728 --> 00:09:54.439
Everyone is upset.

00:09:55.023 --> 00:09:56.608
It's not your fault, Aiko.

00:09:56.983 --> 00:09:58.985
They've protected you so far.

00:09:59.569 --> 00:10:00.570
But...

00:10:02.364 --> 00:10:07.244
In order to protect my team,
I'll kill you two myself.

00:10:10.997 --> 00:10:12.874
Let's trust them.

00:10:19.798 --> 00:10:20.799
What?

00:10:23.301 --> 00:10:24.594
Kanzaki.

00:10:26.221 --> 00:10:28.431
-Kurose.
-<i>Is everyone all right?</i>

00:10:28.515 --> 00:10:30.976
Yes. Do you have any news?

00:10:31.059 --> 00:10:33.520
<i>I have two things. First,</i>

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:38.066
<i>the Matter's activity is linked</i>
<i>to the brainwaves of Yuzuha Isazu,</i>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.527
<i>who's hospitalized in a coma.</i>

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.070
Yuzuha?

00:10:42.362 --> 00:10:44.114
<i>Do you know something about it?</i>

00:10:44.197 --> 00:10:45.031
No.

00:10:45.991 --> 00:10:47.784
I wonder if it has become active.

00:10:48.034 --> 00:10:48.869
What's "it"?

00:10:49.327 --> 00:10:52.247
Did something happen
to Yuzuha after her accident

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.958
when Isazu entrusted her to you?

00:10:55.917 --> 00:10:56.793
What else?

00:10:56.877 --> 00:10:57.836
Hey!

00:10:58.336 --> 00:10:59.296
<i>What else?</i>

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.632
Try to stay calm.

00:11:03.633 --> 00:11:06.344
Dr. Kiryu has died.

00:11:06.678 --> 00:11:09.681
What? Dr. Kiryu is dead?

00:11:10.807 --> 00:11:13.184
<i>Naturally, the new director is Isazu.</i>

00:11:13.935 --> 00:11:15.979
<i>Hey! Are you listening?</i>

00:11:17.981 --> 00:11:20.233
Yuzuha, it's Dad.

00:11:20.775 --> 00:11:23.320
I'm sorry. You must have been lonely.

00:11:24.487 --> 00:11:28.491
I've found a wonderful treasure.

00:11:28.909 --> 00:11:33.413
Records from Duplicate Unit One,

00:11:34.581 --> 00:11:37.667
the first human body
made from artificial organisms.

00:11:47.761 --> 00:11:50.263
Damn it! What's with all this activity?

00:11:50.388 --> 00:11:53.016
I told you we shouldn't move at night!

00:11:53.099 --> 00:11:55.477
Tough luck! Just deal with it!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.063
Stay alert! Don't let them surround us!

00:12:07.113 --> 00:12:09.449
These things don't move like the rest!

00:12:19.501 --> 00:12:22.754
Kanzaki, your aim's not steady.
What's wrong?

00:12:23.421 --> 00:12:24.381
It's nothing!

00:12:27.759 --> 00:12:28.635
Everyone...

00:12:29.219 --> 00:12:30.887
What the hell is that?

00:12:34.975 --> 00:12:37.936
A human form!
But we've never seen one so big.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.397
What? A human form?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.108
That must be the cause
of all this activity!

00:12:51.992 --> 00:12:52.867
Shino!

00:12:53.743 --> 00:12:55.203
We can't retreat!

00:12:55.287 --> 00:12:57.914
We need to drop K4's Guillotine
right away!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.834
Top priority!
Get a sample of this human form Matter!

00:13:01.751 --> 00:13:03.128
Attack from both sides!

00:13:03.211 --> 00:13:04.379
Okay.

00:13:05.755 --> 00:13:07.674
-Forward!
-Wilco!

00:13:09.134 --> 00:13:11.219
<i>You must be curious about it, Yuzuha.</i>

00:13:12.429 --> 00:13:13.805
Well, you see,

00:13:14.014 --> 00:13:18.101
it was information
I found on Dr. Kiryu's computer.

00:13:18.977 --> 00:13:22.564
There were detailed records
of the first duplicate body

00:13:23.023 --> 00:13:25.108
that Dr. Kiryu created.

00:13:26.067 --> 00:13:29.779
It was a few months before
Aiko Tachibana's duplicate body,

00:13:29.863 --> 00:13:31.865
Unit Two was made.

00:13:34.701 --> 00:13:36.327
Haruka, behind you!

00:13:42.417 --> 00:13:43.376
Sagami?

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.004
It's coming after our light.

00:13:46.212 --> 00:13:48.173
Use the girl's power!

00:13:48.548 --> 00:13:50.133
You don't need to tell me!

00:13:51.885 --> 00:13:53.345
Shinoyama, the arm!

00:13:54.429 --> 00:13:56.347
-Where is it?
-<i>Right above you!</i>

00:13:56.931 --> 00:13:57.807
What?

00:14:11.863 --> 00:14:14.449
I got a sample of the human form Matter!

00:14:14.699 --> 00:14:16.117
Sending data now!

00:14:16.618 --> 00:14:17.535
All right!

00:14:17.619 --> 00:14:19.245
Data received!

00:14:19.329 --> 00:14:21.664
Evidence, Oscar 21 Gamma!

00:14:22.248 --> 00:14:24.918
My firepower's down. Cover me!

00:14:25.335 --> 00:14:26.378
Are you okay, Aiko?

00:14:27.045 --> 00:14:28.463
Yes.

00:14:30.673 --> 00:14:35.303
I didn't sense that human form Matter,
and I don't sense its pain.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.138
Why?

00:14:38.056 --> 00:14:40.850
A few years after Unit One was made,

00:14:41.101 --> 00:14:46.731
the original human died with his family
while he was still very young.

00:14:46.815 --> 00:14:50.360
The duplicate body
should have been destroyed at that time.

00:14:50.819 --> 00:14:55.573
We were only allowed to have copies
as long as they could help the original.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.784
But it was not destroyed,

00:14:57.867 --> 00:15:00.495
and continued to live and grow.

00:15:01.788 --> 00:15:03.498
"Duplicate bodies aren't human,

00:15:03.581 --> 00:15:05.667
so it's not a human experiment."

00:15:05.917 --> 00:15:07.502
That's what it said.

00:15:09.212 --> 00:15:10.338
That's absurd.

00:15:11.381 --> 00:15:14.634
While they knew
it could be inhabited with a spirit,

00:15:15.093 --> 00:15:17.429
they treated it like a piece of meat.

00:15:17.637 --> 00:15:19.472
Such arrogance!

00:15:20.473 --> 00:15:22.517
And even more astonishing,

00:15:22.642 --> 00:15:26.104
Unit One was lent out
to another research lab,

00:15:26.563 --> 00:15:28.523
as if it were a guinea pig.

00:15:29.399 --> 00:15:32.026
It was Yura who borrowed it.

00:15:32.735 --> 00:15:34.237
<i>Toshihide Yura.</i>

00:15:34.654 --> 00:15:39.033
<i>It was when he listened to you</i>
<i>playing your violin so well.</i>

00:15:40.952 --> 00:15:42.328
The cartridges are ready.

00:15:42.871 --> 00:15:44.747
I'm sending two packs!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.919
It's Matter!

00:15:50.253 --> 00:15:53.006
How did it get through the Beetle's armor?

00:15:54.382 --> 00:15:56.593
Aiko! Get back to the rear seats!

00:16:00.221 --> 00:16:02.390
The heavy laser is overloading!

00:16:02.974 --> 00:16:04.476
Damn! I can't stop it!

00:16:05.185 --> 00:16:06.519
Evacuate! Hurry!

00:16:06.603 --> 00:16:08.354
-Tachibana!
-Okay!

00:16:32.212 --> 00:16:33.546
Shinoyama...

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.466
Daisuke?

00:16:40.762 --> 00:16:41.804
Daisuke!

00:16:52.732 --> 00:16:53.691
Daisuke!

00:16:53.775 --> 00:16:54.943
Shinoyama!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:56.736
Shino!

00:16:57.737 --> 00:16:59.072
Hang on!

00:16:59.155 --> 00:17:00.406
Maho...

00:17:00.573 --> 00:17:03.535
Deliver... the cartridges.

00:17:03.785 --> 00:17:06.246
Break through, and drop the Guillotine.

00:17:06.329 --> 00:17:07.622
I'll fix you up now!

00:17:09.165 --> 00:17:10.583
Forget it.

00:17:11.292 --> 00:17:14.170
Don't stop. Keep moving.

00:17:15.547 --> 00:17:16.422
Daisuke...

00:17:17.465 --> 00:17:22.303
There's a purpose to what we're doing.

00:17:33.189 --> 00:17:34.232
Shino!

00:17:47.245 --> 00:17:49.414
What are you doing! Run!

00:17:51.249 --> 00:17:53.960
Daisuke! Daisuke!

00:17:54.627 --> 00:17:56.379
Daisuke!

00:18:08.308 --> 00:18:11.019
Pull it together!
We have to deliver these!

00:18:12.687 --> 00:18:14.606
We can't let this end here!

00:18:14.731 --> 00:18:15.565
Hurry!

00:18:35.585 --> 00:18:36.919
Tachibana...

00:18:37.003 --> 00:18:38.838
-What the--?
-Seriously?

00:18:38.921 --> 00:18:40.214
What?

00:18:53.019 --> 00:18:54.812
Stop! Your body can't take it!

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:02.987
Kanzaki!

00:19:04.489 --> 00:19:07.116
I'll deliver the cartridges to the team!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.286
Go to the Guillotine with Aiko
and protect her!

00:19:12.789 --> 00:19:13.998
Let's go, Tachibana!

00:19:15.458 --> 00:19:18.252
It's impossible to stop that giant one!

00:19:19.295 --> 00:19:21.214
Distract it by hitting its head,

00:19:21.297 --> 00:19:23.549
then hit its base to slow it down!

00:19:24.133 --> 00:19:25.635
-Let's go!
-Wilco!

00:19:27.762 --> 00:19:31.182
<i>Right now, AMBREC is in a terrible state.</i>

00:19:36.729 --> 00:19:38.773
Kanzaki! Aiko! This way!

00:19:38.856 --> 00:19:40.942
Tachibana! Tachibana!

00:20:07.301 --> 00:20:08.428
-Now!
-Now!

00:20:15.101 --> 00:20:17.145
<i>The Burst, you see,</i>

00:20:17.645 --> 00:20:20.398
<i>it is what killed Yura.</i>

00:20:21.274 --> 00:20:24.902
<i>Are you sad? Maybe you are.</i>

00:20:28.656 --> 00:20:29.532
<i>But...</i>

00:20:30.533 --> 00:20:34.537
<i>the autopsy was performed</i>
<i>by his boss, Kurose.</i>

00:20:38.332 --> 00:20:45.006
<i>The same day Yura's death was confirmed,</i>
<i>Kurose performed a top-secret surgery.</i>

00:20:45.131 --> 00:20:46.048
<i>Also...</i>

00:20:47.049 --> 00:20:52.054
<i>on the same day, records from Duplicate</i>
<i>Unit One were deleted.</i>

00:20:54.474 --> 00:20:57.393
I'm sorry, Shinoyama.

00:20:58.644 --> 00:20:59.854
I'm so sorry!

00:21:00.855 --> 00:21:03.858
Hey, doesn't this affect you at all?

00:21:04.442 --> 00:21:07.779
Shinoyama died protecting you!

00:21:08.112 --> 00:21:10.573
This is as far as you go, Kanzaki.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:16.496
Remember what I said?
I would do this to protect my team.

00:21:17.121 --> 00:21:19.707
You think this mission can stop the Burst?

00:21:19.791 --> 00:21:21.292
There's no proof it can.

00:21:21.459 --> 00:21:23.920
but Shino bet his life that it could,

00:21:24.545 --> 00:21:25.922
and died for it!

00:21:26.506 --> 00:21:28.466
Pay for it with your life!

00:21:29.967 --> 00:21:31.385
If there were proof,

00:21:31.803 --> 00:21:34.055
there'd be no point
in betting on it.

00:21:34.972 --> 00:21:37.517
What?
How dare you insult Shino!

00:21:38.392 --> 00:21:40.144
Even without any proof,

00:21:41.062 --> 00:21:43.689
Shinoyama believed my story.

00:21:44.565 --> 00:21:47.401
He believed in me.

00:21:52.365 --> 00:21:55.326
I will never go back!

00:21:55.993 --> 00:21:58.204
I will get to Primary Point,

00:21:58.538 --> 00:22:02.959
and prove that there is
a real purpose to this mission!

00:22:04.293 --> 00:22:05.461
Yura's death...

00:22:06.254 --> 00:22:08.965
and the deletion
of the duplicate body's records...

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:12.260
These two events occurred
at the hands of Kurose,

00:22:15.388 --> 00:22:17.306
and they are closely connected.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:18.933
TOSHIHIDE YURA

00:22:19.016 --> 00:22:20.810
Toshihide Yura lives...

00:22:21.561 --> 00:22:26.315
as Duplicate Unit One Yuya Kanzaki.

00:23:57.782 --> 00:23:59.950
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
